Source: hub-managed process `okf-tauri-dev` (`pnpm tauri dev`, env DISPLAY=:99),
cwd = this worktree. Vite dev server became ready ("ready in" matched), then the
first full debug build of the app binary failed at the LINK step. Process was
stopped via hub stop; stop reported `exited exit=1`.

Decisive excerpt of the build log (argv elided where marked; everything else verbatim):

    Building [=======================> ] 426/428: orbitkit                                            error: linking with `cc` failed: exit status: 1
      |
      = note:  "cc" <full linker argv elided here; it included "-lwebkit2gtk-4.1" and "-L" "/hu/lib" and libs -gtk-3 -gdk-3 -lsoup-3.0 -ljavascriptcoregtk-4.1 -lglib-2.0 ...>
      = note: some arguments are omitted. use `--verbose` to show all linker arguments
      = note: warning: unable to open library directory '/hu/lib': FileNotFound
              error: unable to find dynamic system library 'webkit2gtk-4.1' using strategy 'no_fallback'. searched paths:
                src-tauri/target/debug/deps/rustcsrI7de/raw-dylibs/libwebkit2gtk-4.1.so
                /home/megastruktur/.rustup/toolchains/stable-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/rustlib/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/libwebkit2gtk-4.1.so

    Building [=======================> ] 426/428: orbitkit                                            error: could not compile `orbitkit` (lib) due to 1 previous error

Interpretation (see REPORT.md): pkg-config metadata reaches the build through a docker
shim whose library directory /hu/lib exists only inside the shim container; the
sandbox-side linker has no filesystem path to the host's WebKitGTK libraries, so
`-lwebkit2gtk-4.1` cannot resolve. Cargo compilation (check, no linking) succeeds.
